# Chat history logging (mandatory)

This workspace maintains an **observable log** in `diagrams/chat-history/`. New chat sessions must continue it.

## When to log

After any session with **non-trivial work** (code, docs, architecture, troubleshooting, demo changes):

1. **Before ending** — update logs (do not skip if user did not ask).
2. **Each user message** that requests work → one row in `USER-REQUEST-LOG.md` (next `U-0XX` ID).

## Files to update (checklist)

| Step | File | Action |
|------|------|--------|
| 1 | `diagrams/chat-history/USER-REQUEST-LOG.md` | Add rows: ID, category, "You asked", outcome |
| 2 | `diagrams/chat-history/YYYY-MM-DD-topic.md` | Create or append session; include **User requests** table |
| 3 | `diagrams/chat-history/INDEX.md` | Add timeline row if new session day/topic |
| 4 | `diagrams/README.md` | Update chat-history table only if new session file |

Use template: `diagrams/chat-history/_TEMPLATE-session.md`

## Request categories

`discovery` · `architecture` · `implementation` · `demo` · `troubleshooting` · `documentation`

## User request row format

```markdown
| U-0XX | category | Short summary of user question | What was delivered (paths) |
```

## Session sections (agent side)

Goal · User requests · Decisions · Artifacts · Diagrams updated · Open items

## Do not

- Bulk-copy `_intake/` prose into vault or logs
- Create duplicate diagram ASCII in vault — link `diagrams/`

## Onboarding

Read `diagrams/chat-history/INDEX.md` and `AGENTS.md` at repo root when context is unclear.
